# WEEK 6

Harikesh Tamberini and I had a meeting to discuss how to clean our data file. We used PostGre SQL to clean this data. We filtered out 
data where the subject is null and isn't named 'Student Interactions' or 'Search for Teammates!'. We don't want null rows to
affect what we find when we look for the answers to our metrics. We filtered out this subject lines since there were many lines 
of these just with student information and no followup by TA or instructor. We found this to be irrelevant to our future goals. 
Additionally, we filtered out data where the folder was null and the submission_html_removed is null. The 'submission_html_removed'
is the comment section, or the question/answer a student or TA has made on Piazza. We just want to remove as 
many null rows as possible so they do not affect our calculations later in the semester. We also filtered out submission_html_removed
that had a character count of less than 20. We assumed that anything under 20 characters would be irrelevant. 

This is our query:

SELECT * FROM piazza_cs6601_np_anonymized
WHERE (subject IS NOT null) AND 
      (subject NOT LIKE '%Student Interactions%) AND
      (subject NOT LIKE '%Search For Teammates!%) AND
      (folders IS NOT null) AND
      (submission_html_removed IS NOT null) AND
      (length(submission_html_removed) > 20);
      
